@startuml CA4_Data_Flow

!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam roundCorner 10
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho

title CA4 Plant Monitoring System - Data Flow Architecture\nEdge-to-Cloud with VPN Tunnel

' ============================================================================
' EDGE SITE
' ============================================================================
package "Edge Site (Local Machine)" as edge #E8F5E9 {
    
    component "Sensor 1\n(Tomato)" as sensor1 #90EE90
    component "Sensor 2\n(Basil)" as sensor2 #90EE90
    component "Sensor 3\n(Lettuce)" as sensor3 #90EE90
    
    component "WireGuard Client\n10.20.0.2" as vpn_edge #FFE082
    
    note right of sensor1
        **Data Created:**
        Every 10 seconds
        • Moisture: 35-85%
        • Temperature: 15-30°C
        • Light: 200-1000 lux
        • Humidity: 30-85%
        
        Format: JSON
        Destination: Kafka
    end note
}

' ============================================================================
' VPN TUNNEL
' ============================================================================
cloud "VPN Tunnel\n(WireGuard)\n10.20.0.0/24\nEncrypted" as vpn #FFF3E0

' ============================================================================
' CLOUD SITE
' ============================================================================
package "Cloud Site (AWS EC2 - 10.0.0.0/16)" as cloud #E3F2FD {
    
    component "WireGuard Gateway\n10.20.0.1" as vpn_cloud #FFE082
    
    rectangle "Frontend Tier (10.10.1.0/24)" as frontend #E1F5FE {
        component "Home Assistant\nPort 8123" as ha #4FC3F7
    }
    
    rectangle "Messaging Tier (10.10.2.0/24)" as messaging #FFF9C4 {
        component "Zookeeper\nPort 2181" as zk #FFD54F
        component "Kafka\nINT: 9092\nEXT: 9093" as kafka #FFA726
        component "Mosquitto\nPort 1883\n(Also in Frontend\n& Data nets)" as mqtt #FF7043
    }
    
    rectangle "Data Tier (10.10.3.0/24)" as data #E8F5E9 {
        database "MongoDB\nPort 27017" as mongo #66BB6A
    }
    
    rectangle "Application Tier\n(Messaging + Data Networks)" as app_tier #F3E5F5 {
        component "Plant Processor\n(Consumer)" as processor #BA68C8
    }
    
    note right of processor
        **Processor Networks:**
        Connected to BOTH:
        • messaging-net (10.10.2.0/24)
          - To consume from Kafka
        • data-net (10.10.3.0/24)
          - To write to MongoDB
          - To publish to MQTT
        
        **Scalable:**
        Can scale 1→3 replicas
        for load testing
    end note
    
    note right of kafka
        **Kafka Config:**
        Topic: plant-sensors
        Consumer Group: 
          plant-processor-group
        
        **Listeners:**
        • INTERNAL: kafka:9092
          (cloud services)
        • EXTERNAL: 10.20.0.1:9093
          (VPN - edge sensors)
    end note
    
    note right of mongo
        **MongoDB Storage:**
        DB: plant_monitoring
        Collections:
        • sensor_readings
        • plant_configurations
        
        **Document:**
        {
          plantId: "edge-sensor-001"
          timestamp: ISO datetime
          location: "edge-tomato-bed"
          plantType: "tomato"
          sensors: {
            soilMoisture: 57.67
            lightLevel: 640.81
            temperature: 19.21
            humidity: 69.05
          }
        }
    end note
    
    note right of ha
        **Home Assistant:**
        Auto-discovery via MQTT
        
        **Displays:**
        • Real-time sensor values
        • Historical graphs
        • Alert notifications
        • Plant health status
        
        **Topics:**
        homeassistant/sensor/
        {plantId}/{metric}
    end note
}

' ============================================================================
' DATA FLOW
' ============================================================================

sensor1 --> vpn_edge : 1. Generate\nJSON data\n(10s intervals)
sensor2 --> vpn_edge
sensor3 --> vpn_edge

vpn_edge --> vpn : 2. Encrypt\n& Transmit

vpn --> vpn_cloud : 3. Receive\n& Decrypt

vpn_cloud --> kafka : 4. Forward\nto Kafka\n(port 9093)

kafka --> processor : 5. Consume\nMessages\n(partition 0)

processor --> mongo : 6a. Store\nRaw Data\n(INSERT)
processor --> mqtt : 6b. Publish\nEvents

mqtt --> ha : 7. Subscribe\n& Display

zk --> kafka : Coordination

' ============================================================================
' LEGEND
' ============================================================================
legend bottom left
|= **Step** |= **Description** |= **Protocol/Port** |
| 1 | Edge sensors generate readings | JSON over Kafka protocol |
| 2 | Data encrypted via VPN | WireGuard (UDP 51820) |
| 3 | VPN gateway receives data | 10.20.0.1:9093 |
| 4 | Kafka queues messages | Topic: plant-sensors |
| 5 | Processor consumes from Kafka | Consumer group |
| 6a | Raw data stored in MongoDB | TCP 27017 (internal) |
| 6b | Events published to MQTT | TCP 1883 (internal) |
| 7 | Home Assistant displays data | MQTT subscription |

|= **Network** |= **CIDR** |= **Purpose** |
| VPN Tunnel | 10.20.0.0/24 | Site-to-site encryption |
| Frontend | 10.10.1.0/24 | User interfaces |
| Messaging | 10.10.2.0/24 | Message brokers |
| Data | 10.10.3.0/24 | Data storage |
| AWS VPC | 10.0.0.0/16 | Cloud network |

|= **Data Format** |= **Example** |
| Kafka Message | {"plantId":"edge-sensor-001", "timestamp":"2025-12-03T02:12:45Z",\n"location":"edge-tomato-bed", "plantType":"tomato",\n"sensors":{"soilMoisture":57.67, "lightLevel":640.81,\n"temperature":19.21, "humidity":69.05}} |
| MQTT Topic | homeassistant/sensor/edge-sensor-001/moisture/config |
end legend

@enduml
